  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Restoration of Balcad Water Supply</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved health and socio-economic stability for the population of Balcad through increasing access to safe water, on the immediate, medium and long term.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The aim of the project is to provide access to safe drinking water for 42,000 citizens of Balcad, Somalia.The project will upgrade two functional boreholes, restore two unused boreholes and drill another four. Over 75% of the 7,000 households will be connected to tap water by household connections. Water kiosks will be renovated and additional kiosks will be built to provide water for people that cannot afford a house connection.Boreholes, distributions systems and kiosk will be functional and relevant stakeholders will be trained in technicalities and service provision.  Specific attention will be given to the collaboration between the Dutch and Somali public partner, as the latter need capacity in building public tasks, responsibilities and power of authority.</narrative>
  </description>
